<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Select Reverse Scans</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Scan Data &gt; Reverse Scans</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">Sometimes the data quality is slightly affected by the direction in which the sensor is held while capturing data. Call</span> <span class="Command">Select Reverse Scans</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to select parts of a visible scan captured while scanning in reverse direction.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command works on scan data only. Note that it removes any previous scan data selections. Other data types remain unaffected.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">For maximum accuracy, it is recommend to scan in the 'Forward' direction relative to the sensor head. The forward direction is the same direction as moving 'down' in the scan menu, i.e. with the localiser probe ahead of the sensor.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">this command to select reverse scans and then delete them if necessary.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
